  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Extended stretch of dry and seasonable weather\nthis week\n\n10 PM Update...\nDewpoints are recovering over the NW from mid-afternoon depths.\nSome fog is possible tonight in the valleys, but the dryness of\nthe airmass does argue against it. Without real support to \nremove the small mention of patchy fog in the grids, we'll just\nkeep it in there. \n\nPrevious discussion...\nPersistent high pressure over the Northeast U.S. will provide \nan extended stretch of dry and seasonable weather this week. \nTonight won't be as cold as the past few nights have been, but \nwe should still see temperatures drop into the upper 30s and low\n40s. Patchy frost will be possible in the coldest spots, but \nnot in the areas where the growing season is still active. The \nlatest model data shows the dry spell continuing into the final \nweek of October. This rain- free pattern will feature a string \nof sunny and seasonably warm afternoons with low humidity \nfollowed by clear and chilly moonlit nights with areas of frost.",
